#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161698 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162132 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "130d80d7-d0f9-5979-b966-e6c0bf7a27e9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Covariance Using the Definition"}] :question/id #uuid "9716c386-896d-5b3b-a0e6-d6d3d1a83cbf" :question/math-academy-id "e-10348" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.5$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0$ | $0.4$ |\n\nCalculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y$." :question/worked-solution "The covariance of two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint support $S$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Cov}[X, Y] = \\sum_{(x,y)\\in S}(x - \\textrm E[X])(y - \\textrm E[Y])f(x,y)\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y$. These are given by the row and column totals, respectively.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $f_X$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.5$ | $0.6$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0$ | $0.4$ | $0.4$ |\n| $f_Y$ | $0.1$ | $0.9$ | $1$ |\n\nWe now compute $\\textrm{E}[X]$ and $\\textrm{E}[Y]$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE[X] &= ∑_(x ∈ S_{X})x \\cdot f_{X}(x) \\\\\n&= 1 \\cdot 0.6 + 2 \\cdot 0.4 \\\\\n&= 0.6 + 0.8 \\\\\n&= 1.4 \\\\\nE[Y] &= ∑_(y ∈ S_{Y})y \\cdot f_{Y}(y) \\\\\n&= 0 \\cdot 0.1 + 1 \\cdot 0.9 \\\\\n&= 0 + 0.9 \\\\\n&= 0.9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for the covariance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nCov[X, Y] &= ∑_((x, y) ∈ S)(x - E[X])(y - E[Y])f(x, y) \\\\\n&= ∑_((x, y) ∈ S)(x - 1.4)(y - 0.9)f(x, y) \\\\\n&= (1 - 1.4)(0 - 0.9)f(1, 0) \\\\\n&= + (1 - 1.4)(1 - 0.9)f(1, 1) \\\\\n&= + (2 - 1.4)(0 - 0.9)f(2, 0) \\\\\n&= + (2 - 1.4)(1 - 0.9)f(2, 1) \\\\\n&= (-0.4)(-0.9)(0.1) \\\\\n&= + (-0.4)(0.1)(0.5) \\\\\n&= + (0.6)(-0.9)(0) \\\\\n&= + (0.6)(0.1)(0.4) \\\\\n&= 0.04\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161700 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162134 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fab3dcab-d386-5f54-bfba-f2e5951af9ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Covariance Given a Joint Probability Density Function"}] :question/id #uuid "ebf98f0c-765c-5cc4-bfa0-89ffefe450f4" :question/math-academy-id "e-10356" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n${\\frac{3}{5}\\sqrt{x}y,\\begin{vmatrix}0 \\le x \\le 1, 2 \\le y \\le 3, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$.\n\nFind the covariance of $X$ and $Y$." :question/worked-solution "The joint support of $X$ and $Y$ is given by the rectangle\n\n$$\nS = [0,1] \\times [2,3]\n$$\n\nMoreover, we can write\n\n$$\nf(x,y) = g(x) \\cdot h(y)\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\ng(x) =\\dfrac{3}{5} \\sqrt{x}\n$$\n\nand $h(y) =y$.\n\nTherefore, $X$ and $Y$ are independent, and consequently\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Cov}[X,Y] = 0\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161701 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162135 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4549d88-dfbd-57e0-a673-99e394563613" :knowledge-point/title "Stating the Covariance Using the Definition"}] :question/id #uuid "5e69ba34-d7f9-512b-9d53-f00f8f556049" :question/math-academy-id "e-10357" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint support $S=S_X\\times S_Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=5$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $X=1$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.45$ | $0.15$ |\n\nFind an expression for the covariance in sigma notation." :question/worked-solution "The covariance of two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint support $S$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Cov}[X, Y] = \\sum_{(x,y)\\in S}(x - \\textrm E[X])(y - \\textrm E[Y])f(x,y)\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y$. These are given by the row and column totals, respectively.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=5$ | $f_X$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $X=1$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ | $0.4$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.45$ | $0.15$ | $0.6$ |\n| $f_Y$ | $0.6$ | $0.4$ | $1$ |\n\nWe now compute $\\textrm{E}[X]$ and $\\textrm{E}[Y]$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE[X] &= ∑_(x ∈ S_{X})x \\cdot f_{X}(x) \\\\\n&= 1 \\cdot 0.4 + 4 \\cdot 0.6 \\\\\n&= 0.4 + 2.4 \\\\\n&= 2.8 \\\\\nE[Y] &= ∑_(y ∈ S_{Y})y \\cdot f_{Y}(y) \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot 0.6 + 5 \\cdot 0.4 \\\\\n&= 1.2 + 2 \\\\\n&= 3.2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for the covariance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nCov[X, Y] &= ∑_((x, y) ∈ S)(x - E[X])(y - E[Y])f(x, y) \\\\\n&= ∑_((x, y) ∈ S)(x - 2.8)(y - 3.2)f(x, y)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161702 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162136 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "929a4b02-6c3d-59ce-b774-7ca6487077ff" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Covariance Using the Shortcut Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "08ae7ab0-00d9-51db-9c5d-d3b13ddaedac" :question/math-academy-id "e-10358" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $X=1$ | $0.2$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.4$ | $0.2$ |\n\nIf $\\textrm{E} [X]=2.8$ and $\\textrm{E}[Y] = 2.4$, calculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y$." :question/worked-solution "The covariance of $X$ and $Y$ can be calculated using the formula\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Cov}[X,Y] = \\textrm{E} [XY] - \\textrm{E}[X]\\cdot \\textrm{E}[Y]\n$$\n\nWe use the rule of the lazy statistician to find $\\textrm{E}[XY]$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE[XY] &= ∑_((x, y) ∈ S)xy \\cdot f(x, y) \\\\\n&= (1)(2)(0.2) + (1)(3)(0.2) + (4)(2)(0.4) + (4)(3)(0.2) \\\\\n&= 6.6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the covariance formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nCov[X, Y] &= E[XY] - E[X] \\cdot E[Y] \\\\\n&= 6.6 - (2.8)(2.4) \\\\\n&=-0.12\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162422 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162136 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "929a4b02-6c3d-59ce-b774-7ca6487077ff" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Covariance Using the Shortcut Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82b061aa-a562-5cec-b12f-b031e6b197d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159735} {:answer/id #uuid "9dc50379-a73f-56f1-a77e-1b9ac7f0f5e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159736} {:answer/id #uuid "bf1e623d-3883-51ff-9be3-842a410c8835" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159737} {:answer/id #uuid "06809080-8efa-5670-a26b-998d5dc4f55a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159738} {:answer/id #uuid "3b7115c8-ba08-5aac-b629-621bf83dee7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159739}] :answer-field/id #uuid "b1eacff7-d507-52b8-80a6-7de096999f8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159734}] :question/id #uuid "e37b553f-54ac-5d84-b352-476c36a3f396" :question/math-academy-id "q-146149" :question/problem "If $E[X] = 20$, $E[Y] = 2$, and $E[XY] = 44.8$ for two random variables $X$ and $Y$, calculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y$.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162429 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162134 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fab3dcab-d386-5f54-bfba-f2e5951af9ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Covariance Given a Joint Probability Density Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9808b13b-2fee-56b6-a014-1a93e20b5b91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159777} {:answer/id #uuid "e0aa279a-fbf4-566c-a2e5-90c94f02f018" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159778} {:answer/id #uuid "eadf298b-3043-50fd-acb0-90abef3abd34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159779} {:answer/id #uuid "0974ef81-d76c-5bb3-b890-13e356d506c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159780} {:answer/id #uuid "4975ae33-06ab-5386-bc3d-6d44edc8ba9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159781}] :answer-field/id #uuid "316d0a76-34fa-5862-a104-987d7995c329" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159776}] :question/id #uuid "3f486e7e-5dfa-501f-90c2-497028f8a357" :question/math-academy-id "q-146266" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$f(x, y) = {e^{-x - y},\\begin{vmatrix}x > 0, y > 0, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$.\n\nFind the covariance of $X$ and $Y$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162445 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162135 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4549d88-dfbd-57e0-a673-99e394563613" :knowledge-point/title "Stating the Covariance Using the Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92816af4-0c70-5a6a-8b94-854320a1548d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∑_((x, y) ∈ S)(x - 3.8)(y - 1.96)f(x, y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159873} {:answer/id #uuid "efe9ef9a-70ec-526c-b030-86dbeac05f5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∑_((x, y) ∈ S)x(y - 1)f(x, y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159874} {:answer/id #uuid "f6841ecd-0074-58fd-b57b-562f0dfbc325" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∑_((x, y) ∈ S)(x - 1.96)(y - 3.8)f(x, y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159875} {:answer/id #uuid "f70f8b02-733d-54de-92f9-44d0a9305940" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∑_((x, y) ∈ S)(x - 1)(y - 2)f(x, y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159876} {:answer/id #uuid "21019cb9-4a48-550a-99b7-893ad3830709" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∑_((x, y) ∈ S)(xy - 1.96)f(x, y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159877}] :answer-field/id #uuid "ee0ffc3c-5e92-543d-a922-72f19b24c70c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159872}] :question/id #uuid "30db451b-93c6-5bae-8115-d6afd25f7fca" :question/math-academy-id "q-147920" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function $f(x, y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint support $S = S_{X} \\cdot S_{Y}$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y = 2$ | $Y = 5$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $X = 1$ | $0.12$ | $0.4$ |\n| $X = 3$ | $0.28$ | $0.2$ |\n\nWhich of the following gives the covariance of $X$ and $Y$?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411854 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162134 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fab3dcab-d386-5f54-bfba-f2e5951af9ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Covariance Given a Joint Probability Density Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "964c5bc4-7a2e-5bae-85a7-d482c6e36e48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411756} {:answer/id #uuid "a758ee1c-9dab-5058-8a43-ffb91581708b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411765} {:answer/id #uuid "c3bca5a5-b1a9-54bd-8c07-941077c325cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{17}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411785} {:answer/id #uuid "e2b6fede-844a-5216-ae74-664077e8f2bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411805} {:answer/id #uuid "f1b661e8-65e7-5407-8292-c4496fc2965b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411812}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2b6fede-844a-5216-ae74-664077e8f2bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411805} :answer-field/id #uuid "dee10a7b-d9ae-5a81-b136-732cb3456d2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411847}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1994bb13-7165-5891-a83f-5e7560b1da72" :question/math-academy-id "q-147946" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{8}(x+{y}^{2}),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{5}{4}$ and $\\text{E}[Y]=\\frac{9}{16},$ calculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The covariance of $X$ and $Y$ can be calculated using the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nTo find $\\text{E}[XY],$ we use the rule of the lazy statistician:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}xyf(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}xy\\cdot \\frac{3}{8}(x+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{8}y{\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}+x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{8}y{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{y}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{8}y[\\frac{8}{3}+2{y}^{2}]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(y+\\frac{3}{4}{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}+\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the covariance formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{16}-(\\frac{5}{4})(\\frac{9}{16}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{64}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
